card c05
kind: teach
type: explain
scored: 0
title: Isotope does not mean radioactive
figure: isotope-stability
figure_at: 2

body:
    An isotope is just a version of an element. It does not mean the atom is [[radioactivity|radioactive]]. Carbon-12 and carbon-13 are stable. Carbon-14 is not. Most of the atoms around you are stable isotopes.

